{"body": "This PR adds Stage 1 support for Iceberg-managed SQL scalar UDFs in Spark 4.1, backed by the Iceberg REST catalog (list/load endpoints):\n\nread-only scope: list + load + execute only (no CREATE/REPLACE/DROP).\nExecution model: Spark executes by loading the SQL body/spec and using the analyzer rewrite, not session-scoped temp registration.\nOut of scope for now: named args, default args, UDTF/TVF, full CRUD.\n\nFollow-up PRs:\n\nwrite support stopgap, before Spark SPI: Spark procedure-based DDL stopgap (create/replace/drop via procedures) that calls REST catalog CRUD endpoints once they exist.\nREST catalog CRUD + governance: REST catalog CREATE/REPLACE/DROP endpoints + request/response types + error mapping + Concurrency/idempotency semantics (ETag / If-Match, Idempotency-Key behavior), and authorization docs/tests.\nafter Spark lands CodeLiteralFunctionCatalog: Implement Spark’s CodeLiteralFunctionCatalog against the REST catalog endpoints", "date": "2026-01-02T20:37:02Z", "hash": "sha256:46e4159846b09edc52f6", "id": "gh:apache/iceberg#14954", "meta": {"additions": 2540, "base": "main", "comments": 5, "deletions": 5, "draft": false, "files": ["api/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/exceptions/NoSuchFunctionException.java", "core/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/rest/Endpoint.java", "core/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/rest/RESTCatalog.java", "core/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/rest/RESTSessionCatalog.java", "core/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/rest/ResourcePaths.java", "core/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/rest/functions/RestFunctionService.java", "core/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/rest/responses/ListFunctionsResponse.java", "core/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/rest/responses/LoadFunctionResponse.java", "core/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/udf/UdfSpecResolver.java", "core/src/test/java/org/apache/iceberg/rest/RESTCatalogAdapter.java", "core/src/test/java/org/apache/iceberg/rest/Route.java", "core/src/test/java/org/apache/iceberg/rest/TestRESTFunctions.java", "core/src/test/java/org/apache/iceberg/rest/functions/TestRestFunctionService.java", "open-api/rest-catalog-open-api.py", "open-api/rest-catalog-open-api.yaml", "open-api/src/testFixtures/java/org/apache/iceberg/rest/RESTCatalogServer.java", "open-api/src/testFixtures/java/org/apache/iceberg/rest/RESTServerExtension.java", "spark/v4.1/spark-extensions/src/main/scala/org/apache/iceberg/spark/extensions/IcebergSparkSessionExtensions.scala", "spark/v4.1/spark-extensions/src/main/scala/org/apache/iceberg/spark/extensions/RewriteSqlFunctions.scala", "spark/v4.1/spark-extensions/src/test/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/extensions/TestRestScalarFunctionCatalog.java", "spark/v4.1/spark-extensions/src/test/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/extensions/TestSqlFunctionAnalyzerRewrite.java", "spark/v4.1/spark/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/BaseCatalog.java", "spark/v4.1/spark/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/udf/IcebergSqlUdfScalarFunction.java", "spark/v4.1/spark/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/udf/SqlFunctionCatalog.java", "spark/v4.1/spark/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/udf/SqlFunctionSpec.java", "spark/v4.1/spark/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/udf/SqlFunctionSpecParser.java", "spark/v4.1/spark/src/main/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/udf/SqlUdfCatalogFunction.java", "spark/v4.1/spark/src/test/java/org/apache/iceberg/spark/TestBaseWithCatalog.java"], "labels": ["API", "spark", "core", "stale", "OPENAPI"], "n_files": 28, "number": 14954, "repo": "apache/iceberg", "reviews": [{"at": "2026-01-29T23:01:36Z", "by": "flyrain", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2026-01-29T23:03:01Z", "by": "flyrain", "state": "COMMENTED"}, {"at": "2026-01-29T23:03:43Z", "by": "flyrain", "state": "COMMENTED"}], "state": "open", "thumbs_up": 0, "updated_at": "2026-11-13T03:03:06Z"}, "people": ["huaxingao"], "refs": [], "source": "github", "title": "SQL UDF support Stage 1", "type": "pr", "url": "https://github.com/apache/iceberg/pull/14954"}
{"body": "This PR adds support for Apache Spark 4.2.0.\nRelease publishing: Spark 4.2 artifacts are excluded from dev/stage-binaries.sh and will not be published by default.\nThe first two commits rename the Spark 4.1 module to 4.2 and then restore 4.1 so Git retains file history. The remaining commits contain the Spark 4.2 compatibility changes and review follow-ups.\nChanges\n\nAdds and registers the Spark 4.2 modules in Gradle, settings, packaging, benchmarks, CI, and CVE scanning.\nIntegrates Spark 4.2's RelationCatalog and View APIs while preserving Iceberg property-only updates for view properties, including cached and session catalogs.\nUpdates view validation and metadata handling for Spark-owned view expansion, catalog-qualified cycle detection and output, compatibility with existing Iceberg views, metric-view dependencies, and de-duplicated table/view listings.\nConverts geospatial values between Spark's BinaryView representation and Iceberg's pure WKB Parquet representation, including StructInternalRow and nested values.\nUpdates Spark 4.2 tests, benchmarks, APIs, and error expectations, and resolves the released Spark 4.2.0 artifacts from Maven Central.\n\nGeospatial compatibility details\n\nValidate WKB during Spark conversion: Spark 4.2 parses and validates WKB when constructing Geometry and Geography values. It accepts the seven OGC base geometry types, including Z/M variants, and enforces longitude and latitude bounds for geography. Existing Iceberg data with extended geometry types or out-of-bounds geography coordinates can now fail with wkbParseError instead of passing through as it did in Spark 4.1. POINT EMPTY remains accepted. Iceberg uses Spark's public conversion API and cannot bypass this validation.\nKeep nested geospatial conversion in the Spark 4.2 module: Spark 4.2 requires nested geometry and geography values to use its BinaryView physical representation, so arrays, maps, and structs must convert Iceberg WKB values explicitly. Older Spark versions use different physical types and can be handled separately.\n\nView compatibility details\n\nAdapt to Spark 4.2's view and relation APIs: Spark 4.2 requires catalogs that provide both tables and views to implement RelationCatalog. It also represents query text, current catalog and namespace, schema mode, SQL configs, dependencies, and properties through its new View model. SparkCatalog and SparkSessionCatalog translate that model to and from Iceberg view metadata and implement create, replace, create-or-replace, load, drop, and rename through the new signatures.\nUse Spark-owned view expansion: ResolveRelations now calls RelationCatalog.loadRelation before extension resolution rules, and BaseCatalog.loadRelation falls back from tables to views. Spark therefore expands Iceberg views into logical View nodes and applies GetViewColumnByNameAndOrdinal plus schema-mode-driven casting. This replaces Iceberg 4.1's positional expansion. The unreachable ResolveViews relation expansion and its identifier rewrites have been removed; Spark function resolution now owns references such as system.bucket.\nRoute Iceberg commands around session-catalog fallbacks: Spark's ResolveSessionCatalog exits early or selects V1 handling for several view commands. RewriteViewCommands recognizes only Iceberg-backed V2 view catalogs before that happens, while preserving local and global temporary-view behavior, and routes create, drop, rename, describe, show-create, show-properties, and show-views commands to Iceberg-aware logical and physical nodes. Resolved commands carry the already-loaded view into inspection planning, avoiding a second catalog lookup.\nRestore validation and cycle detection: Rewriting CreateView means Spark's native CheckViewReferences no longer sees the original node. CheckViews explicitly reuses Spark's checks for temporary objects, generated aliases, and column counts, and traverses Spark logical View nodes for fully qualified recursive-view detection. Iceberg 